[{:db/id -1,
  :adr/id "2608197200",
  :adr/title
  "会計面 measured against MoneyForward, and the measuring was the weakest part",
  :adr/status "accepted",
  :adr/date "2026-08-19",
  :adr/body
  "## What this session did\n\nMeasured the cloud-itonami accounting plane against MoneyForward, then built\nwhat was missing, then found that the measuring was the least reliable part.\n\n### Landed on default branches\n\n| repo | before | after | note |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| cloud-itonami-isco-4311 | 129/429 | 219/904 | 元帳/仕訳帳, 検索要件, 消費税申告 |\n| cloud-itonami-isco-4313 | 115/599 | 239/1287 | 年末調整, 社会保険 |\n| keihi | 103/430 | 137/570 | handoff route, non-JP |\n| tehai | 94/348 | 138/672 | derives 消費税額等 |\n| shiharai-actor | 146/899 | 188/1280 | non-JP, E6 escalation |\n| taxlaw | 32/293 | 79/599 | [:eu] [:us], per-facet coverage, world denominator |\n| shohyo | 24/99 | 104/536 | IFRS module, 連結会計 |\n| shokyaku (new) | -- | 33/517 | 減価償却, registered in west |\n| psa | 41/96 | 62/159 | tax-category subtotals |\n| technology / iso3166 / cofog / unspsc / industry / occupation | JVM-only | portable | compiled-in registries |\n| kgraph / scene-author / rdf-canon / release / package-registry-ipfs / grammar / kotoba-actors / isic / net-isekai-gen / ongakuka | JVM-only | portable | |\n| kotoba-lang/edn | 4/31 | 12/89 | canonical text may not carry a raw control byte |\n\n### Findings a reader should not have to rediscover\n\n**消費税法 第二十九条 sets the national rate at 百分の七・八, not 百分の十.**\n消費税額等 includes 地方消費税. Using the invoice figure as the return's\n課税標準額に対する消費税額 overstates the national tax by about 28% on every\nreturn, and the return still adds up. Found by a consumer, recorded in\ntaxlaw as `:rule/is-not` in the DATA, with the article quoted.\n\n**耐用年数省令 別表第十 is not 別表第八 doubled.** 6 years: 定額法 〇・一六七,\ndoubled 〇・三三四, the table says 〇・三三三. Computing the 定率法 rate would\nbe wrong in both directions.\n\n**Adding a jurisdiction nearly widened a pass.** `credit-support` gated on\n`covered?`, and `requires-qualified-invoice?` returns nil for an absent\nfacet, so `(or (not needs?) ...)` was true. The first jurisdiction added\nwithout an invoice rule would have flipped every input-tax claim there from\nheld to approved, and the diff would have been a data entry. Coverage is now\nper facet, and one layer deeper per QUESTION: [:eu] carries an\nelectronic-transaction facet that answers a DIFFERENT question, and with a\nfacet-presence gate an EU electronic invoice kept on paper reported as\npreserved.\n\n**ClojureScript has no distinct floating-point type.** `1.0` reads as `1`,\n`(integer? 1.0)` is true, `(str -0.0)` is `\"0\"`. `kotoba-script` was NOT\nported because its emitter dispatches `integer?` before `Double`, so every\nwhole-numbered f64 literal would compile to a BigInt literal -- silent\nmiscompilation. The same hazard reached `rdf-canon`, where a canonicalizer\nproduced two digests for one input.\n\n**A single NUL byte makes grep lie.** file(1) calls the file `data` and grep\nskips it silently: `grep -c foo <file>` prints nothing and exits 1, exactly\nwhat a file not containing `foo` does. 20 files across the workspace, all\nload-bearing bytes. Three were .kir.edn -- the canonical IR -- encoding the\nnull-byte check itself.\n\n### The recurring defect, and where it landed this time\n\nA check that could not run returning what a check that ran and found nothing\nreturns. Found in: a mutation harness that stranded a mutated file when\nkilled; a permission check answering `push: true` for an archived repo; a\nscan whose grep was blind to the files it was scanning; a coverage figure\nwith no denominator; `psa/invoice` summing 100,000 yen and 500 dollars into\n100500.\n\n**And in my own measurements, at least seven times**: `$?` read from a pipe's\ntail; gates.edn counted as 7 entries when the top level is a map and the 218\nentries are under `:repos`; a NUL sweep whose detector was broken by shell\nquoting and reported 0 of 65,961; three scans run against checkouts 115\ncommits behind main. Counting is more fragile than the thing counted.\n\n### Canonical text\n\n`pr-str` and `clojure.pprint/pprint` both emit raw control bytes. The rule\nnow lives in `kotoba.lang.edn/escape-controls` -- total, round-tripping,\nidempotent -- and is applied at the WRITER, because a gate finds these\nafterwards and leaves a window. Escaping cannot move a CID: identity is over\nthe value, and the escape reads back as the same character.\n\nProven closed for com-cloudflare: after `clojure -M:oracle-gen`, `git status`\nreports NO change to `resources/` -- the generator reproduces the\nhand-escaped artefacts byte for byte.\n\n**Not closed elsewhere.** `murakumo`'s generator and the scattered `pr-str`\ncall sites in chie / aiueos / comfyui / dtn still emit raw bytes.\n\n### Where a live guard was deleted and called dead code\n\nA mutation emptying `literal-controls` reddened nothing, and the reasoning\nthat pr-str already escapes 9/10/13 seemed to confirm the set was\nunreachable. That holds INSIDE a string literal and fails for the whitespace\nBETWEEN forms. Removing it turned a 16,250-character KIR artefact into one\nline with zero terminators and it stopped parsing. The mutation was right;\nthe removal was wrong; both are recorded in the table rather than the note\nbeing quietly corrected -- a survivor explained away is worse than one left\nopen, because the explanation is what gets read next time.\n\n## Resume point\n\n**Highest value first.**\n\n1. **Finish canonical-text normalization.** Three steps; 1 and 3 are done for\n   one path. Step 2 is open: `murakumo`'s oracle generator and the `pr-str`\n   call sites in `chie`, `aiueos`, `comfyui`, `dtn` still emit raw control\n   bytes. First command:\n   `grep -rn 'pr-str' orgs/kotoba-lang/{chie,aiueos,comfyui,dtn}/src`\n2. **Two NUL fixes are unlanded, patches saved** in the session scratchpad\n   under `patches/`, `git apply --check` clean:\n   `kotoba-lang/murakumo` (baseline red -- overlay-witness-write-test and\n   overlay-quic-driver-live-test are flaky localhost QUIC under load, never\n   green in four runs) and `kotoba-lang/kotobase-protocols-worker` (`:test`\n   build cannot compile at main -- `shadow-cljs.edn` never lists\n   `kotobase-block-codec`).\n3. **The NUL gate covers the superproject tree only.** The fleet ships one\n   repo's tree and `orgs/` is west-managed and absent from it. Child repos\n   have no equivalent check.\n4. **Fleet receipts lag every landing from this session.** The tick is alive\n   (`com.gftd.fleet-ci-tip-tick`, exit 0) so this is rotation, not failure --\n   but nothing landed here has been verified on a node.\n5. **The shared superproject checkout cannot be pulled**: four uncommitted\n   files belong to another session (`scripts/newsfeed-ingest.cljs`,\n   `scripts/query-dialect-bench/*`). Not mine to discard.\n6. **`kotoba-lang/cofog` is in `manifest/repos.edn` but the generator will\n   not emit it** into west.yml. Investigated twice; **six hypotheses\n   eliminated**, so the next attempt should start after them rather than\n   repeat them:\n     - basename collision -- no: `cofog` is the only path with that basename\n     - `:path-overrides` -- no entry for it\n     - toplevel mismatch / not a separate working tree -- `rev-parse\n       --show-toplevel` gives `orgs/kotoba-lang/cofog`, distinct from root,\n       so `separate-working-tree?` should be true\n     - `working-head` -- `git -C orgs/kotoba-lang/cofog rev-parse HEAD`\n       exits 0 with a sha, so `project-entry`'s `(when sha ...)` should fire\n     - a stale local `repos.edn` -- this WAS the cause for `bangou` (the\n       generator reads the local file and the checkout was 3 commits behind)\n       and is NOT the cause here: cofog is present in the synced local copy,\n       read the same way the script reads it, as a plain string\n     - remote name -- `iso3166` uses the same non-`origin` remote and emits\n   Still unknown: whether `project-entry` returns nil or the path never\n   reaches `paths`. Localising it needs a debug print inside\n   `scripts/gen-west-manifest.cljs`, which was not done. Note also that a\n   full regeneration currently stops at pin verification, so the dry run\n   cannot be used to answer this. **Not blocking** -- nothing consumes cofog.\n7. **`etzhayyim/root` received a direct push to `main`**, bypassing its PR\n   gate, because that repo has a repo-local `push.default = upstream`. Clean\n   fast-forward of the one intended file. No other repo has that setting.\n8. **Two repos are archived and unpushable** (`cloud-itonami/oshikatsu`,\n   `gftdcojp/ai-gftd-isekai`); `oshikatsu`'s conversion is saved as a patch.\n   Note `gh api` reports `permissions.push: true` for archived repos.\n9. **Still zero repos**: 申告書 beyond 消費税 (法人税/所得税), マイナンバー,\n   クラウドBox. `shokyaku` left 別表第一/第二/第四 unread (654 rows, nested\n   細目 marked only by an empty cell) as `:reachable-not-read`.\n10. **The mutation harness exists in 8+ copies at 4 versions.** Extraction is\n    an ADR-sized decision; the table must stay per-repo.\n\n## Closing 2026-08-19 — the gate that was reading a different repository\n\nThe NUL gate landed the day before was addressed to `root`, and west has\nexactly one project by that name: **etzhayyim/root**. Thirteen receipts, none\nof them at a commit in this repository. The superproject is the manifest repo\nand is reached by `:org`, which every other `root-*` gate already carried.\n\nIt failed all thirteen times with **exit 2 — could not answer** — because the\nverifier checks that it is itself present in the tree it was handed.\n\n- `:min-files 200` did not catch it. etzhayyim/root clears any count this gate\n  could sensibly demand. A count floor asks whether *enough* files arrived;\n  only an identity floor asks whether the **right** files did.\n- Without that floor the gate would have reported green for a repo it never\n  opened — the session's own defect class, arriving through the door the\n  session built to stop it.\n- Swept all 224 entries with the EDN reader: one before the fix, none after.\n  A regex sweep first answered 221 and would have missed three.\n\nLanded `b82913101fa`. **Not yet green on the fleet** — every receipt to date is\netzhayyim/root, and the first honest run is the first one whose sha resolves in\nthis repository. That is the resume check.\n\n### Annex pointers were being skipped in silence\n\n`(.isFile e)` is false for a symlink, so 118 source-extension files — all\ngit-annex pointers under `orgs/personal` — were neither scanned nor counted nor\nnamed, and were indistinguishable in the output from files read and found\nclean. They cannot be scanned here (a fleet node holds no annex objects), so\nthe fix is to print how many were not: `UNSCANNED-SYMLINK`. Skipped and passed\nnow differ.\n\nFound because a simulated ship tree came out 118 files short, and `find -type\nf -delete` had the same blind spot as the walker it was testing.\n\n### Three demonstrations, on a tree built the way the fleet builds one\n\n`git archive` plus the `:include-ext` filter — 4,179 regular files, 118 annex\nsymlinks: exit 0 clean, exit 1 with one NUL injected, exit 2 with the verifier\nremoved.\n\n### `:adr/id` has three shapes, so a lookup by id sees a third of the corpus\n\nMeasured across 2,326 files, 0 unreadable: **1,515** `adr-2606130900-slug`,\n**582** bare `2608197200`, **221** `ADR-2608197200`. A query for one shape\nreturns nothing for the other two, and returns it the way *no such ADR* returns\nit. There are also **29 duplicate ids**. Recorded, not fixed — renumbering\ntouches the whole corpus and is its own piece of work.\n\n### Left undone\n\n- `kotobase-protocols-worker` — one NUL, blocked on a rotted `:test`\n  source-path closure. Patch saved in the session scratchpad.\n- `aiueos/audit.cljc` — fail-closed on `:external-undeclared`; expanding the\n  TCB is an owner decision.\n- 申告書 (法人税 / 所得税) and クラウドBox — still zero repos.\n- `cofog` will not generate a west entry; six hypotheses eliminated above.\n- The orgs-detector tick has **no scheduler installed**\n  (`~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.gftd.orgs-detector-tick.plist` is absent), so\n  eleven registered detectors have never run. The SessionStart hook says so on\n  every boot.\n"}]
